  "question": {
    "text": "The density (in $\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ ) of the metal which forms a cubic close packed (ccp) lattice with an axial distance (edge length) equal to 400 pm is $\\qquad$ .\nUse: Atomic mass of metal $=105.6 \\mathrm{amu}$ and Avogadro's constant $=6 \\times 10^{23} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "11",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { CCP : } \\\\ & (\\mathrm{Z}=4, \\mathrm{a}=400 \\mathrm{pm}, \\mathrm{M}=105.6 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}) \\\\ & \\text { Density }=\\frac{\\mathrm{Z} \\times \\mathrm{M}}{\\mathrm{a}^3 \\times \\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{A}}} \\\\ & =\\frac{4 \\times 105.6}{\\left(400 \\times 10^{-10}\\right)^3 \\times 6 \\times 10^{23}}=11.00 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{cm}^3\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}